# Extend Cursor rules

`.cursor/rules/` is the standing memory for this repo. Chat is not.

When you learn something that the next agent will need (workflow, build/test pitfalls, load semantics, package boundaries, “do not do X”), **write it down**:

- **Update** the matching rule in `.claude/rules/` if the topic already exists.
- **Create** a new `.claude/rules/<topic>.md` with `paths:` set if it is a distinct concern (one topic per file, keep it short and actionable).
- Mirror every change to the matching `.mdc` in `.cursor/rules/` (new rule → new `.mdc` with `globs:` set to the same paths), as `CLAUDE.md` describes. Use `alwaysApply: true` only for repo-wide workflow (how to build, run, test).
- Do not dump a one-off bugfix into a rule. Do record the reusable constraint that would have prevented the bug.

Do this in the same session you learned it. Do not wait for the user to ask.
